1
00:00:02,290 --> 00:00:03,750
So thanks for coming by, guys.

2
00:00:03,920 --> 00:00:07,170
We wanted to bounce some ideas off of you about the wedding ceremony.

3
00:00:07,340 --> 00:00:08,790
Oh.

4
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:12,010
What's the matter? Are you okay?

5
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:12,010
Yeah, it's just...

6
00:00:12,170 --> 00:00:14,720
Monica said "wedding."

7
00:00:15,050 --> 00:00:18,640
Uh, so we wanted to know if one of you would like to read something.

8
00:00:18,810 --> 00:00:22,430
Okay, yeah, I guess I can do that too.

9
00:00:23,850 --> 00:00:25,350
Too?

10
00:00:25,980 --> 00:00:29,480
Yeah, I kind of, ahem, have something else planned for you guys.

11
00:00:29,650 --> 00:00:32,570
Do you mind telling us what it is?

12
00:00:29,650 --> 00:00:32,570
Sorry.

13
00:00:32,740 --> 00:00:35,990
I'm kind of keeping this one on the QT.

14
00:00:36,160 --> 00:00:38,820
Well, whatever it is, I hope it involves winking.

15
00:00:41,290 --> 00:00:42,750
Hey.

16
00:00:41,290 --> 00:00:42,750
Hey.

17
00:00:42,910 --> 00:00:45,040
So I talked to one of the DOOL writers...

18
00:00:45,210 --> 00:00:47,290
What is DOOL?

19
00:00:45,210 --> 00:00:47,290
Days Of Our Lives.

20
00:00:49,340 --> 00:00:53,170
You're not gonna believe it. My character is coming out of his coma!

21
00:00:53,340 --> 00:00:55,010
That's wonderful.

22
00:00:53,340 --> 00:00:55,010
Wow, Joey.

23
00:00:55,180 --> 00:00:59,260
And not only that. I'm getting a new brain!

24
00:01:00,180 --> 00:01:04,480
So great things are happening at work and in your personal life.

25
00:01:05,140 --> 00:01:07,270
What do you mean you're getting a new brain?

26
00:01:07,440 --> 00:01:10,360
They're killing off one of the characters, and when she dies...

27
00:01:10,520 --> 00:01:13,320
...and her brain is being transplanted into my body.

28
00:01:14,900 --> 00:01:18,700
Heh, what? A brain transplant?

29
00:01:18,870 --> 00:01:20,490
It's ridiculous.

30
00:01:20,660 --> 00:01:24,200
I think it's ridiculous that you haven't had sex in three and a half months.

31
00:01:28,630 --> 00:01:32,380
It's winter. There are fewer people on the street.

32
00:01:33,800 --> 00:01:35,130
Who are they killing off?

33
00:01:35,300 --> 00:01:37,800
Uh, Cecilia Monroe. She plays Jessica Lockhart.

34
00:01:38,050 --> 00:01:39,760
No!

35
00:01:38,050 --> 00:01:39,760
No!

36
00:01:40,220 --> 00:01:43,810
She is so good at throwing drinks in people's faces.

37
00:01:44,060 --> 00:01:46,730
I don't think I've ever seen her finish a beverage.

38
00:01:46,980 --> 00:01:49,650
The way she slaps people. Wouldn't you love to do that?

39
00:01:49,810 --> 00:01:51,270
Don't do it.

40
00:01:52,110 --> 00:01:53,980
And she's been on the show forever.

41
00:01:54,150 --> 00:01:56,940
It's gonna be really hard to fill her shoes.

42
00:01:54,150 --> 00:01:56,940
Yeah.

43
00:01:57,110 --> 00:01:58,570
Help me out here. When you...

44
00:01:58,740 --> 00:02:03,240
When you come out of the "brain transplant"...

45
00:02:03,410 --> 00:02:06,160
...you are going to be her?

46
00:02:06,330 --> 00:02:09,250
Yes, but in Drake Ramoray's body.

47
00:02:12,170 --> 00:02:15,750
Why is this so hard for you to get? I thought you were a scientist.

48
00:02:54,750 --> 00:02:56,500
Rach, so that guy there:

49
00:02:56,750 --> 00:02:57,840
Straight or gay?

50
00:02:59,220 --> 00:03:00,550
Oh.

51
00:03:00,720 --> 00:03:03,680
Oh, yeah, he's too cute to be straight. Ha, ha.

52
00:03:05,140 --> 00:03:07,220
Ooh, Knockers will help us figure it out.

53
00:03:12,940 --> 00:03:14,650
All right, straight.

54
00:03:15,440 --> 00:03:17,650
And not subtle.

55
00:03:19,530 --> 00:03:21,450
He left his cell phone.

56
00:03:19,530 --> 00:03:21,450
Oh?

57
00:03:21,610 --> 00:03:24,360
We could hand it to Gunther, he'll put it in lost and found.

58
00:03:24,530 --> 00:03:28,080
Or we could use it to call China, see how those guys are doing.

59
00:03:28,790 --> 00:03:32,790
What if, uh, he calls his own cell phone to find out who found it, and I answer...

60
00:03:32,960 --> 00:03:35,580
...and we start talking and we fell in love?

61
00:03:35,790 --> 00:03:37,960
Wouldn't that be a great story?

62
00:03:38,210 --> 00:03:41,720
Kind of like a fairy tale for the digital age.

63
00:03:38,210 --> 00:03:41,720
Yeah.

64
00:03:41,880 --> 00:03:44,050
That does sound great. I'm gonna get the phone.

65
00:03:44,260 --> 00:03:47,550
What? Wait. Why do you get the story?

66
00:03:47,760 --> 00:03:50,470
I don't know. I haven't been out on a date in so long.

67
00:03:50,730 --> 00:03:53,190
Phoebe, you had a date three days ago.

68
00:03:53,440 --> 00:03:58,020
That wasn't a date. That was friends getting together and having sex.

69
00:03:58,270 --> 00:04:00,400
Okay. Great. See, I get the phone.

70
00:04:00,570 --> 00:04:03,820
No way. You just broke up with Tag a week ago.

71
00:04:03,990 --> 00:04:09,280
Yeah, and until now, I didn't think I would love again.

72
00:04:10,290 --> 00:04:11,580
Nice try.

73
00:04:10,290 --> 00:04:11,580
Hey, wait.

74
00:04:11,830 --> 00:04:14,960
How do we fairly decide who gets the phone?

75
00:04:15,120 --> 00:04:16,960
I don't know.

76
00:04:22,050 --> 00:04:23,220
Well, um...

77
00:04:23,930 --> 00:04:26,340
Maybe we could, uh...

78
00:04:27,510 --> 00:04:30,100
Ah-ha! Too slow! Ha-ha-ha.

79
00:04:31,020 --> 00:04:33,640
Ah-ha! Too cocky.

80
00:04:38,060 --> 00:04:40,480
I'm going to date him. There's nothing you can do.

81
00:04:40,690 --> 00:04:41,780
Yes, there is.

82
00:04:41,940 --> 00:04:45,150
What, are you going to kill him like you did Charles?

83
00:04:47,160 --> 00:04:49,990
Oh, my baby.

84
00:04:54,410 --> 00:04:55,830
Cut!

85
00:05:00,040 --> 00:05:04,590
That was a great scene. And that slap looked so real. How do you do that?

86
00:05:04,800 --> 00:05:08,430
Oh, just years of experience.

87
00:05:04,800 --> 00:05:08,430
Can I get some ice here?

88
00:05:10,180 --> 00:05:12,930
Anyway, I just wanted to say how wonderful I think you are.

89
00:05:13,350 --> 00:05:15,850
You're not the fan who's dying, are you?

90
00:05:16,310 --> 00:05:20,060
No, uh, I'm Joey Tribbiani. We did a scene together yesterday.

91
00:05:20,270 --> 00:05:23,650
I'm the guy in the coma.

92
00:05:20,270 --> 00:05:23,650
Oh, that was a real person?

93
00:05:26,150 --> 00:05:30,030
I wanted to say, since I'm getting your brain when you leave the show...

94
00:05:30,200 --> 00:05:33,410
...I was wondering if there was any tips...

95
00:05:30,200 --> 00:05:33,410
I'm leaving the show?

96
00:05:33,580 --> 00:05:35,870
I don't know, why? Did you hear something?

97
00:05:37,540 --> 00:05:40,080
Who told you that?

98
00:05:37,540 --> 00:05:40,080
Oh, uh...

99
00:05:40,250 --> 00:05:43,500
One of the writers.

100
00:05:40,250 --> 00:05:43,500
Which? Was it bald or was it tall?

101
00:05:44,510 --> 00:05:47,670
You know, it doesn't matter, because it is not true.

102
00:05:47,840 --> 00:05:48,970
Okay. Whoo, eh.

103
00:05:49,220 --> 00:05:52,890
And if it were true, how dare you come to me and ask me for tips...

104
00:05:53,100 --> 00:05:55,850
...about a character I've been playing for 20 years!

105
00:06:01,230 --> 00:06:04,440
Miss Monroe... Oh, there you go.

106
00:06:08,240 --> 00:06:09,570
Okay, look, I have an idea.

107
00:06:09,780 --> 00:06:13,580
Why don't we see what kind of numbers he has on his speed dial?

108
00:06:13,740 --> 00:06:16,790
And then from that, we can tell who has more in common with him...

109
00:06:16,950 --> 00:06:18,870
...and whoever does gets the phone.

110
00:06:19,540 --> 00:06:22,330
Fine. All right.

111
00:06:19,540 --> 00:06:22,330
All right.

112
00:06:22,670 --> 00:06:25,880
First name on the speed dial is "Mom."

113
00:06:22,670 --> 00:06:25,880
Oh.

114
00:06:26,050 --> 00:06:28,920
I lost my mom to suicide.

115
00:06:29,090 --> 00:06:30,180
Okay, no way.

116
00:06:30,340 --> 00:06:33,050
You can't use that to get the cute guy and the last muffin.

117
00:06:33,220 --> 00:06:36,140
Did I use that already today? I'm sorry.

118
00:06:37,230 --> 00:06:40,690
"Ben, Carlos, David..."

119
00:06:40,850 --> 00:06:43,860
Oh, I win. He's got Barney's on his speed dial.

120
00:06:44,020 --> 00:06:46,360
So? You don't know that it's Barney's the store.

121
00:06:46,530 --> 00:06:49,490
That could be his friend's house, or a bar, or...

122
00:06:49,650 --> 00:06:52,240
Who has Barney's the store on their speed dial?

123
00:06:52,410 --> 00:06:54,570
His new girlfriend.

124
00:07:08,630 --> 00:07:09,920
What is that?

125
00:07:10,090 --> 00:07:12,840
I think it's the Dying Cat Parade.

126
00:07:14,970 --> 00:07:17,850
Sounds like it's coming from across the street.

127
00:07:18,020 --> 00:07:21,440
Oh, my God.

128
00:07:18,020 --> 00:07:21,440
What?

129
00:07:21,600 --> 00:07:23,900
The thing that Ross was gonna do at our wedding?

130
00:07:24,150 --> 00:07:28,360
He was hanging out with me yesterday and he said, "You're half Scottish, right?"

131
00:07:28,530 --> 00:07:31,820
No. There is no way. It cannot be Ross.

132
00:07:39,790 --> 00:07:43,420
Unbelievable. Why is your family Scottish?

133
00:07:44,830 --> 00:07:47,590
Why is your family Ross?

134
00:07:49,130 --> 00:07:52,260
He cannot play at our wedding. Everyone will leave.

135
00:07:52,430 --> 00:07:55,300
I mean, come on. That is just noise!

136
00:07:55,470 --> 00:07:57,390
It's not even a song.

137
00:07:57,970 --> 00:08:01,180
Wait. If you listen very carefully, I think...

138
00:08:01,350 --> 00:08:04,140
...it's "Celebration" by Kool and the Gang.

139
00:08:10,230 --> 00:08:13,360
You're absolutely right. They are writing me out of the show.

140
00:08:13,530 --> 00:08:17,160
They don't know exactly when it's going to happen, but apparently it's soon...

141
00:08:17,330 --> 00:08:18,830
...and then that's it.

142
00:08:18,990 --> 00:08:22,120
I'm sorry. If it was up to me, you would never leave the show.

143
00:08:22,290 --> 00:08:24,290
Yeah, thanks.

144
00:08:22,290 --> 00:08:24,290
No, I mean it.

145
00:08:24,460 --> 00:08:27,790
I can't believe they'd do this to you. And to your fans.

146
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:32,380
They're gonna be devastated. Heartbroken. They love you so much.

147
00:08:33,010 --> 00:08:34,880
Oh, you're right.

148
00:08:35,550 --> 00:08:36,800
Thank you.

149
00:08:37,050 --> 00:08:38,850
What's your name again?

150
00:08:39,970 --> 00:08:41,810
Joey.

151
00:08:39,970 --> 00:08:41,810
Joey. Well, thank you.

152
00:08:41,970 --> 00:08:44,600
That is so sweet. Oh.

153
00:08:44,770 --> 00:08:47,190
The... The only reason I came up to you before...

154
00:08:47,360 --> 00:08:49,230
...was because, well...

155
00:08:49,480 --> 00:08:52,610
...because I'm really nervous about being you.

156
00:08:52,780 --> 00:08:56,570
You know, if you could help me capture the essence of the character.

157
00:08:56,740 --> 00:08:59,700
Help me keep Jessica alive. Please?

158
00:09:02,160 --> 00:09:03,700
All right, Joey, I will help you.

159
00:09:03,870 --> 00:09:07,420
Not because I owe it to this stupid show...

160
00:09:07,580 --> 00:09:10,840
...but because I owe it to Jessica.

161
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:13,880
Oh, that's great. Thank you so much.

162
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:13,880
You're so welcome.

163
00:09:14,050 --> 00:09:16,760
I've been watching some tapes. How's this?

164
00:09:17,640 --> 00:09:21,100
Jessica Lockhart will never step foot in this place again!

165
00:09:21,260 --> 00:09:22,600
Ever!

166
00:09:24,480 --> 00:09:28,690
Oh, but, Jessica doesn't have an English accent.

167
00:09:28,900 --> 00:09:31,020
I can do an English accent?

168
00:09:33,150 --> 00:09:35,150
That baby's going on my resume.

169
00:09:39,620 --> 00:09:41,660
Hi, Pheebs. How are you?

170
00:09:39,620 --> 00:09:41,660
Good.

171
00:09:41,830 --> 00:09:44,580
Um, Phoebe, remember when we were in the coffeehouse...

172
00:09:44,750 --> 00:09:47,870
...we decided I was gonna keep the cute guy's phone?

173
00:09:48,040 --> 00:09:50,580
Yeah.

174
00:09:48,040 --> 00:09:50,580
And I was gonna keep it in my purse...

175
00:09:50,750 --> 00:09:53,550
...so if it rang, I could just pick it up?

176
00:09:53,710 --> 00:09:58,130
And then do you remember going into my purse and stealing the phone?

177
00:09:59,590 --> 00:10:00,970
Ooh, now you lost me.

178
00:10:01,140 --> 00:10:03,600
You stole the phone.

179
00:10:01,140 --> 00:10:03,600
No, I didn't.

180
00:10:03,760 --> 00:10:06,810
No? So you're saying that if I called it, it wouldn't ring?

181
00:10:06,980 --> 00:10:08,140
No.

182
00:10:06,980 --> 00:10:08,140
Hmm. Okay.

183
00:10:08,310 --> 00:10:11,980
But while you dial, let me show you the features of my new ringing handbag.

184
00:10:12,150 --> 00:10:13,190
Mm.

185
00:10:14,690 --> 00:10:16,650
Oh, it does work.

186
00:10:18,070 --> 00:10:20,070
Phoebe.

187
00:10:18,070 --> 00:10:20,070
That is a different phone.

188
00:10:20,240 --> 00:10:24,910
Oh, is it? Hello. Yes, hi. Is Rachel there?

189
00:10:25,080 --> 00:10:28,620
Yes, she is. Just one moment, please. It's for me!

190
00:10:30,630 --> 00:10:32,420
That is damning evidence.

191
00:10:34,460 --> 00:10:37,670
Oh, my God. I bet that's him.

192
00:10:37,840 --> 00:10:40,180
My digital fairy tale's about to begin.

193
00:10:41,340 --> 00:10:42,760
It's ri...

194
00:10:42,930 --> 00:10:45,140
Would you stop doing that?

195
00:10:45,310 --> 00:10:48,310
Hello? Yes, I'm the one who found your phone.

196
00:10:48,480 --> 00:10:51,100
Phoebe, you can't do th...

197
00:10:48,480 --> 00:10:51,100
Shh, I'm on a call.

198
00:10:53,310 --> 00:10:57,280
Well, yeah, I mean, you could pick it up tonight. Say, 8:30?

199
00:10:57,440 --> 00:11:00,240
At my apartment. It's, um...

200
00:11:00,400 --> 00:11:03,950
It's, um, 5 Morton Street, apartment 14.

201
00:11:04,120 --> 00:11:08,370
And then maybe, you know, after, we could grab a bite to eat or whatever.

202
00:11:08,540 --> 00:11:11,040
Okay. Okay, I'll see you then. Bye.

203
00:11:13,420 --> 00:11:16,040
You do know that I will be here when he comes over.

204
00:11:16,210 --> 00:11:18,460
Oh, and how will you know what time to come over?

205
00:11:18,630 --> 00:11:20,970
You just said it.

206
00:11:23,970 --> 00:11:25,180
Oh.

207
00:11:28,560 --> 00:11:33,520
Joey, the essence of the character is rooted in her confidence.

208
00:11:33,690 --> 00:11:37,320
So when Jessica enters a room, for instance...

209
00:11:37,480 --> 00:11:39,530
...she owns everything...

210
00:11:39,690 --> 00:11:43,570
...and every person in that room.

211
00:11:44,870 --> 00:11:46,660
You try it.

212
00:11:44,870 --> 00:11:46,660
Okay.

213
00:11:54,920 --> 00:11:57,000
Right. Well, he's not mad at the room.

214
00:11:58,300 --> 00:12:01,420
Try it again. He owns it. He owns the room.

215
00:12:01,590 --> 00:12:06,260
It is his. He owns, owns, owns the room! He owns it!

216
00:12:06,930 --> 00:12:09,180
It's a little weird, but it's getting better.

217
00:12:11,100 --> 00:12:15,270
Oh, I'm gonna miss this woman so much. I don't know what I'm gonna do.

218
00:12:15,440 --> 00:12:17,940
It's been 20 years of my life.

219
00:12:18,110 --> 00:12:22,110
Hey, hey. Maybe... Maybe, uh... Maybe this is a good thing.

220
00:12:22,280 --> 00:12:26,160
You know? Lt'll give you a chance to shake things up. Play different characters.

221
00:12:26,320 --> 00:12:27,820
You're so talented.

222
00:12:27,990 --> 00:12:32,580
Probably should've just left years ago when the offers were pouring in...

223
00:12:32,750 --> 00:12:35,620
...but, you know, I just got so comfy here and...

224
00:12:35,790 --> 00:12:38,670
Ugh, I turned down some amazing work.

225
00:12:38,840 --> 00:12:41,130
Like what?

226
00:12:38,840 --> 00:12:41,130
Well...

227
00:12:41,300 --> 00:12:43,880
...let's just say if I'd left 15 years ago...

228
00:12:44,050 --> 00:12:48,800
...the landscape of Mexican cinema would be very different today.

229
00:12:50,770 --> 00:12:52,470
Wow.

230
00:12:53,890 --> 00:12:58,940
But, well, now... Now's a different time for me.

231
00:13:00,780 --> 00:13:04,780
Oh, hey, come on. Don't, uh... Don't do this.

232
00:13:05,030 --> 00:13:07,280
Let me tell you something, okay?

233
00:13:07,530 --> 00:13:12,080
When I watch you do a scene, I'm thinking, "Boy, she is a great actress."

234
00:13:12,240 --> 00:13:16,710
But... But I'm also thinking, "She is hot."

235
00:13:19,290 --> 00:13:21,380
You think I'm hot?

236
00:13:22,710 --> 00:13:24,630
You own the room.

237
00:13:29,010 --> 00:13:31,050
We... We should probably get the...

238
00:13:31,220 --> 00:13:33,470
Oh, yeah. Yeah, we should get...

239
