Do you want some shortbread? It's Scottish, like you are.

252
00:14:40,170 --> 00:14:44,290
Oh, no, thanks. I don't like anything from my Scottish heritage.

253
00:14:44,550 --> 00:14:46,050
What?

254
00:14:46,710 --> 00:14:50,720
Well, it's just that my entire family was run out of Scotland by...

255
00:14:51,930 --> 00:14:53,510
...Vikings.

256
00:14:54,350 --> 00:14:59,140
It sounds to me like your family's ready to, uh, rediscover its Scottish roots.

257
00:14:59,390 --> 00:15:01,690
You can't play bagpipes at the wedding!

258
00:15:03,230 --> 00:15:04,770
How did you know about that?

259
00:15:04,940 --> 00:15:07,280
We heard you play all the way from your apartment.

260
00:15:07,440 --> 00:15:09,780
Were you the ones who called the cops?

261
00:15:11,030 --> 00:15:13,320
That's not really important right now. Ahem.

262
00:15:13,490 --> 00:15:17,080
What is important is, while we appreciate the gesture...

263
00:15:17,290 --> 00:15:21,460
...we just don't feel that bagpipes are appropriate for our wedding.

264
00:15:21,710 --> 00:15:25,290
Why not?

265
00:15:21,710 --> 00:15:25,290
Because we hate them.

266
00:15:25,460 --> 00:15:29,300
Just give me a chance to perform for you, and then decide whatever you want.

267
00:15:29,470 --> 00:15:33,050
I'm not gonna tell you what song I'm gonna play, either. But, uh...

268
00:15:33,220 --> 00:15:35,090
...let's just say when it's over...

269
00:15:35,260 --> 00:15:39,100
...I'll bet there'll be a wee bit o' celebration.

270
00:15:46,230 --> 00:15:48,020
Hey, hey!

271
00:15:49,690 --> 00:15:51,820
Who is it?

272
00:15:51,990 --> 00:15:53,030
Hi, It's Tom.

273
00:15:53,200 --> 00:15:55,070
I'm here to pick up the phone.

274
00:15:53,200 --> 00:15:55,070
Ah!

275
00:15:56,120 --> 00:15:58,490
Whoa, why do you get to answer the door?

276
00:15:58,660 --> 00:16:01,500
Why shouldn't I?

277
00:15:58,660 --> 00:16:01,500
Because it's my apartment.

278
00:16:01,660 --> 00:16:03,870
Well, then I get to give him the phone.

279
00:16:04,040 --> 00:16:07,420
Okay. Good luck explaining all the calls to China.

280
00:16:10,420 --> 00:16:11,710
Hi.

281
00:16:15,800 --> 00:16:18,100
Wow, how long were we arguing for?

282
00:16:21,140 --> 00:16:22,520
Um, ha, ha.

283
00:16:22,690 --> 00:16:24,940
You're not the man who left the cell phone.

284
00:16:25,100 --> 00:16:28,230
No, that's my assistant.

285
00:16:25,100 --> 00:16:28,230
Is he coming?

286
00:16:28,400 --> 00:16:30,690
Um, no.

287
00:16:30,860 --> 00:16:33,320
Could you, uh, give us one second?

288
00:16:33,490 --> 00:16:36,030
Sure.

289
00:16:33,490 --> 00:16:36,030
We'll be right back, sir.

290
00:16:37,490 --> 00:16:41,120
Well, what do we do?

291
00:16:37,490 --> 00:16:41,120
I don't know.

292
00:16:41,290 --> 00:16:42,620
Can you believe this?

293
00:16:42,790 --> 00:16:46,040
We were waiting for a hot guy and an even hotter one shows up.

294
00:16:46,210 --> 00:16:47,920
I know...

295
00:16:51,550 --> 00:16:53,010
What?

296
00:16:53,170 --> 00:16:54,340
Rachel, listen...

297
00:16:54,510 --> 00:16:58,720
...if you let me have him, then I will really owe you one.

298
00:17:00,310 --> 00:17:02,220
All right.

299
00:17:04,100 --> 00:17:06,390
All right, Phoebe, I will let you have him.

300
00:17:06,650 --> 00:17:08,770
But you owe me. You owe me big.

301
00:17:08,940 --> 00:17:12,480
So which one of you lovely ladies am I gonna take to dinner, huh?

302
00:17:12,650 --> 00:17:14,820
Oh, that'd be me, sir.

303
00:17:16,030 --> 00:17:18,200
After you.

304
00:17:16,030 --> 00:17:18,200
Okay, thank you.

305
00:17:19,620 --> 00:17:20,990
Nice.

306
00:17:26,500 --> 00:17:29,880
Well, you certainly own that room.

307
00:17:31,960 --> 00:17:33,550
Actually, I rent the whole place.

308
00:17:33,710 --> 00:17:36,050
And I just got what you meant. Thank you.

309
00:17:39,220 --> 00:17:40,800
Hi.

310
00:17:39,220 --> 00:17:40,800
Hey.

311
00:17:42,350 --> 00:17:45,890
Oh, my God.

312
00:17:46,060 --> 00:17:50,400
Aah! Jessica Lockhart! In my apartment!

313
00:17:50,560 --> 00:17:53,900
I am such a huge fan. I am such a huge fan.

314
00:17:54,070 --> 00:17:55,490
Well, it's nice to know that...

315
00:17:55,650 --> 00:17:58,200
Monica! Monica!

316
00:17:58,740 --> 00:18:01,200
That, uh... That's my roommate, Rachel.

317
00:18:01,370 --> 00:18:03,490
Oh, that explains all the women's underwear.

318
00:18:03,660 --> 00:18:05,330
Sure. Yeah.

319
00:18:06,000 --> 00:18:09,120
Oh, my God, it's true!

320
00:18:10,170 --> 00:18:11,460
Oh, my God.

321
00:18:11,630 --> 00:18:14,800
Can I just ask you to do me... Aw... . Just one favor?

322
00:18:14,960 --> 00:18:16,460
Certainly.

323
00:18:16,630 --> 00:18:19,510
Would you slap me? Would you slap me right here in the face?

324
00:18:21,140 --> 00:18:24,260
I'd love to, but my lawyer said I can't do that anymore.

325
00:18:26,310 --> 00:18:28,350
All right, here we go.

326
00:18:26,310 --> 00:18:28,350
Okay.

327
00:18:28,520 --> 00:18:31,560
No, wait. Just one moment. Um...

328
00:18:32,730 --> 00:18:34,980
You're a stupid bitch.

329
00:18:32,730 --> 00:18:34,980
I really can't slap you.

330
00:18:36,990 --> 00:18:40,530
My God, you're great.

331
00:18:36,990 --> 00:18:40,530
Thanks for stopping by. See you.

332
00:18:42,320 --> 00:18:44,530
I am so sorry about that.

333
00:18:42,320 --> 00:18:44,530
Oh, no, no, no.

334
00:18:44,700 --> 00:18:47,660
Being adored, I'm used to it. Don't worry about it.

335
00:18:48,870 --> 00:18:50,540
Oh, my God.

336
00:18:48,870 --> 00:18:50,540
What?

337
00:18:50,710 --> 00:18:53,710
They sent me today's script. They never send me the script.

338
00:18:53,880 --> 00:18:56,090
They don't?

339
00:18:53,880 --> 00:18:56,090
Well, no, I'm in a coma.

340
00:18:56,260 --> 00:18:58,670
This must mean I have lines.

341
00:19:00,340 --> 00:19:01,970
Oh.

342
00:19:02,930 --> 00:19:04,720
How does it happen?

343
00:19:07,310 --> 00:19:08,640
Ooh.

344
00:19:08,810 --> 00:19:12,440
You get thrown from a horse into an electric fence.

345
00:19:14,310 --> 00:19:16,690
A what? Jessica hates horses.

346
00:19:16,860 --> 00:19:20,780
I'm guessing after this she's not gonna be crazy about electricity, either.

347
00:19:25,620 --> 00:19:29,500
Loosening the saddle on Mother's horse was brilliant, Fredrick.

348
00:19:29,660 --> 00:19:32,210
And the electric fence, inspired.

349
00:19:32,370 --> 00:19:33,790
Thank you, sweetheart.

350
00:19:34,750 --> 00:19:37,170
I can't believe she's really gone.

351
00:19:37,750 --> 00:19:40,460
Look around you. All of this is ours.

352
00:19:40,630 --> 00:19:42,550
I don't think so.

353
00:19:47,600 --> 00:19:48,810
Who are you?

354
00:19:48,970 --> 00:19:50,810
What's the matter, Dina?

355
00:19:50,980 --> 00:19:53,770
Don't you recognize your own...

356
00:19:53,940 --> 00:19:55,400
...mother?

357
00:19:58,360 --> 00:20:01,070
Cut! That was great, everybody. Thank you.

358
00:20:01,240 --> 00:20:03,610
That was so wonderful!

359
00:20:03,780 --> 00:20:07,200
Oh, I think that you're a better Jessica than I ever was.

360
00:20:07,370 --> 00:20:10,240
Oh, no.

361
00:20:07,370 --> 00:20:10,240
Of course not, but you were very good.

362
00:20:10,410 --> 00:20:11,660
Heh, thanks.

363
00:20:11,830 --> 00:20:14,210
Guess what? Good news. I got another job.

364
00:20:14,370 --> 00:20:16,790
Great. Hey, all right! What is it?

365
00:20:16,960 --> 00:20:19,300
A film in Guadalajara.

366
00:20:20,260 --> 00:20:22,050
The airport?

367
00:20:23,880 --> 00:20:25,510
No, that's LaGuardia.

368
00:20:29,220 --> 00:20:32,560
This is Mexico.

369
00:20:29,220 --> 00:20:32,560
Oh, wow.

370
00:20:32,810 --> 00:20:35,100
Well, how long will you be gone?

371
00:20:35,270 --> 00:20:37,190
Eight months.

372
00:20:38,020 --> 00:20:41,690
That's a really long time.

373
00:20:38,020 --> 00:20:41,690
Yeah, but you could come and visit me.

374
00:20:41,860 --> 00:20:46,200
I bet that you could, uh, own a few places down there.

375
00:20:46,950 --> 00:20:51,080
Oh, you know, I should probably buy a place in the city first.

376
00:20:53,120 --> 00:20:55,410
And I just got what you meant. That is a...

377
00:20:55,580 --> 00:20:58,330
I'll tell you, that's a tricky one.

378
00:20:55,580 --> 00:20:58,330
It's a tricky one.

379
00:20:58,500 --> 00:21:00,040
Well...

380
00:21:02,210 --> 00:21:03,460
Good luck.

381
00:21:04,220 --> 00:21:05,800
You too.

382
00:21:21,110 --> 00:21:24,860
Ahem. Okay, now, uh, remember, I'm still learning.

383
00:21:34,580 --> 00:21:36,790
One, two, three, four!

384
00:21:54,980 --> 00:21:57,480
You know the song. Sing along.

385
00:22:14,700 --> 00:22:15,910
So?

386
00:22:16,620 --> 00:22:17,790
No!

387
00:22:16,620 --> 00:22:17,790
No!

